# More info: https://docs.docker.com/engine/reference/builder/#dockerignore-file
# Ignore build and test binaries.
bin/

# Git metadata is not a build input. The binary is built from a file
# list rather than a package path, so go stamps no VCS information
# whatever is here -- `go version -m` reports the build as
# command-line-arguments. Keeping it out also lets the build run from a
# git worktree, where .git is a file naming a directory outside the
# build context: copied in, it points nowhere, and every git call in
# the build fails with "not a git repository".
.git
